request.description:
WebSocket connection for real-time notifications.

Connect: ws://<host>/ws/notifications/?token=<JWT_access_token>

On connect server sends:
  { "type": "unread_count", "count": 3 }

Server pushes on new notification:
  { "type": "new_notification", "notification": { "id", "title", "body", "notification_type", "created_at" } }

Channel groups by role:
  Store Manager:     store_notifications_{store_id}
  Delivery Partner:  delivery_partner_{partner_id}
  Customer:          customer_{user_id}

Events by role:
  Store Manager:     new_order, support_request
  Delivery Partner:  order_assigned
  Customer:          order_update, support_reply, wallet_update

Update order delivery status. Order must be out_for_delivery before marking delivered.

Payload by status:
  delivered:   { "status": "delivered", "latitude": 26.91, "longitude": 75.78, "delivery_notes": "", "override_location": false }
    -> Without override: lat/lng must be within 200m of delivery address
    -> With override_location=true: 200m check is skipped — current coords are still logged in order timeline for audit

  delivered (override):  { "status": "delivered", "latitude": 26.91, "longitude": 75.78, "override_location": true }
    -> Use when partner cannot get within 200m (gated society, wrong pin, etc.)
    -> Always send lat/lng alongside override so coordinates are recorded

  failed:      { "status": "failed", "failure_reason": "Customer not available" }
  cancelled:   { "status": "cancelled", "cancellation_reason": "Customer refused delivery" }

